Modifications in this redistribution (benshi-esp32-sim)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

This is a MODIFIED version of armel/uv-k1-k5v3-firmware-custom. The
upstream commit / tag used is recorded in README.md and in the .bin
filename (v5.9.0 / 435192e at the time of writing).

Files added by benshi-esp32-sim contributors, 2026 (Apache-2.0):

    App/app/host.c    (from firmware/uv-k1-k5v3/patch/host.c)
    App/app/host.h    (from firmware/uv-k1-k5v3/patch/host.h)

Upstream files modified by benshi-esp32-sim contributors, 2026
(see firmware/uv-k1-k5v3/patch/integration.md for the exact diff):

    App/app/app.c        - suspend the radio loop while host mode is active
    App/app/uart.c       - #include host.h + 7 dispatch cases (0x0630..0x0636)
    App/CMakeLists.txt   - enable_feature(ENABLE_HOST_MODE app/host.c)
    CMakePresets.json    - "ENABLE_HOST_MODE": false default

The "host mode" lets an external serial controller suspend the firmware's
own radio servicing and drive frequency / VFO / memory / modulation /
CTCSS / PTT through high-level commands. Build options:
-DENABLE_HOST_MODE=ON -DENABLE_UART_RW_BK_REGS=ON
-DVERSION_STRING_2=v<upstream>.H<rev>  (the ".H<rev>" suffix marks this
build in the on-screen version string and the 0x0514 reply).
